### ============================================
### RESERVAS DE SALONES — REST Client
### ============================================
### Primero haz login para obtener el token.
### POST http://localhost:8000/api/auth/login
### Content-Type: application/json
###
### {"user": "1193377218", "pass": "1193377218"}
### ============================================

### 1. CREAR reserva — exitoso
POST http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id_salon": 2,
    "fecha_reserva": "2026-07-21",
    "hora_reserva": 1,
    "id_user": 3123,
    "portatil": 1,
    "sonido": true,
    "titulo": "Clase de matemáticas",
    "detalle_reserva": "Se necesita proyector y sonido"
}

### 2. CREAR reserva — salón inexistente (debe fallar 400)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id_salon": 9999,
    "fecha_reserva": "2026-07-20",
    "hora_reserva": 1,
    "id_user": 3123
}

### 3. CREAR reserva — salón ya ocupado (debe fallar 400)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id_salon": 1,
    "fecha_reserva": "2026-07-20",
    "hora_reserva": 1,
    "id_user": 3123
}

### 4. CREAR reserva — misma fecha de hoy (debe fallar 400)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id_salon": 1,
    "fecha_reserva": "2026-07-09",
    "hora_reserva": 1,
    "id_user": 3123
}

### 5. CREAR reserva — sin campos obligatorios (debe fallar 400)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "titulo": "Faltan campos"
}

### 6. CREAR reserva — portátiles exceden capacidad del salón (debe fallar 400)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id_salon": 1,
    "fecha_reserva": "2026-07-20",
    "hora_reserva": 1,
    "id_user": 3123,
    "portatil": 999
}

### 7. CREAR reserva — usuario inexistente (debe fallar 400)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id_salon": 1,
    "fecha_reserva": "2026-07-20",
    "hora_reserva": 1,
    "id_user": 99999
}

### ============================================
### ACTUALIZAR / CANCELAR RESERVA
### ============================================

### 8. ACTUALIZAR reserva — cambiar título
PUT http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id": 1,
    "titulo": "Clase de ciencias",
    "detalle_reserva": "Se cambió el detalle"
}

### 9. ACTUALIZAR reserva — cambiar salón y hora
PUT http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id": 128859,
    "id_salon": 2,
    "hora_reserva": 3
}

### 10. ACTUALIZAR reserva — portátil no debería cambiar (se ignora)
PUT http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id": 1,
    "portatil": 5,
    "sonido": true
}

### 11. ACTUALIZAR reserva — ID inexistente (debe fallar 404)
PUT http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id": 99999,
    "titulo": "No existe"
}

### 12. CANCELAR reserva
PUT http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id": 1,
    "cancelar": true
}

### 13. CANCELAR reserva — ya cancelada (debe fallar o no hacer nada)
PUT http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id": 1,
    "cancelar": true
}

### ============================================
### LISTAR RESERVAS
### ============================================

### 14. LISTAR todas las reservas (paginadas)
GET http://localhost:8000/api/reservas?per_page=5

### 15. LISTAR reservas por usuario
GET http://localhost:8000/api/reservas?id_user=3123

### 16. LISTAR reservas por salón
GET http://localhost:8000/api/reservas?id_salon=2

### 17. LISTAR reservas por fecha
GET http://localhost:8000/api/reservas?fecha_reserva=2026-01-22

### 18. LISTAR reservas canceladas
GET http://localhost:8000/api/reservas?cancelado=true

### 19. LISTAR reservas activas (no canceladas)
GET http://localhost:8000/api/reservas?cancelado=false

### 20. LISTAR reservas — combinación de filtros
GET http://localhost:8000/api/reservas?id_user=3123&id_salon=2&cancelado=false&per_page=3

### ============================================
### CREACIÓN MÚLTIPLE (BATCH)
### ============================================

### 21. CREAR reservas múltiples — distintas horas mismo día
POST http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id_salon": 2,
    "fecha_reserva": "2026-07-22",
    "hora_reserva": [1, 2, 3],
    "id_user": 3123,
    "portatil": 1,
    "titulo": "Clase multiple - mismo día"
}

### 22. CREAR reservas múltiples — distintos días misma hora
POST http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id_salon": 2,
    "fecha_reserva": ["2026-07-23", "2026-07-24", "2026-07-25"],
    "hora_reserva": 1,
    "id_user": 3123,
    "titulo": "Clase multiple - mismos días"
}

### 23. CREAR reservas múltiples — varios días y varias horas
POST http://localhost:8000/api/reservas
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "id_salon": 2,
    "fecha_reserva": ["2026-07-28", "2026-07-29"],
    "hora_reserva": [1, 2],
    "id_user": 3123,
    "portatil": 1,
    "titulo": "Clase multiple - combinatoria"
}
